@startuml
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #888888
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #ffffff
  ArrowColor #000000
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #fffde0
  BorderColor #b5b045
}
skinparam participant {
  FontSize 13
}
title <size:20>Joining a challenge — synchronous path (Gateway → Eureka → ms4-challenge-service)</size>\n<size:12><color:#555555>Ahmed (household owner, household #12) joins the challenge #3 “Cut 10 % this month” from the web app.</color></size>

participant "**Client app**\nrole HOUSEHOLD_OWNER" as C #f5f5f5
participant "<color:white>**API Gateway**</color>\n<color:white>:8080</color>" as G #1ba1e2
participant "**Eureka Server**\n:8761" as E #fad7ac
participant "**challenges**\nMS4 · :8084" as CH #ffe6cc
database "**challenge_db**\nMongoDB" as DB #d5e8d4

note over G, DB #fffde0
**0** · At start-up every service registers in Eureka (heartbeat every 30 s) and keeps a cached copy of the registry.
end note

C -> G : **1** · POST /api/v1/challenges/3/participations\n{householdId: 12} + Bearer JWT
activate G
G -> G : **2** · check the JWT (Keycloak keys, role HOUSEHOLD_OWNER / HOUSEHOLD_MEMBER)\nroute /api/v1/challenges/** → lb://ms4-challenge-service
G -> E : **3** · where is ms4-challenge-service?
E --> G : instances (cached registry)
G -> CH : **4** · forward to one instance (load balancing)
activate CH
CH -> CH : **5** · is household 12 in the JWT claim household_ids?\n(MS4 calls no other service: else 403)
CH -> CH : **6** · business rules: challenge ACTIVE and open?\nalready joined? (else 409)
CH -> DB : **7** · INSERT participation (JOINED, progressPct = 0)
DB --> CH : id = p-81
CH --> G : **8** · 201 Created · Location: /api/v1/participations/p-81
deactivate CH
G --> C : 201 Created + ParticipationResponse
deactivate G

note over C
**Error cases**
• 401 / 403 at the gateway: missing token / wrong role
• 403: household not in the caller’s household_ids claim
• 404: challenge not found
• 409: challenge ended / not open, or household already joined
• 503: no instance of MS4 in Eureka (service stopped)
end note
note over DB, CH
**What to remember**
• Steps 1 → 8 are **synchronous**: the client waits for every call.
• Eureka is a **directory, not a proxy**: requests go straight to the chosen instance.
• MS4 has **no synchronous dependency**: ownership comes from the JWT, like MS3.
• MS4 stores only **householdId** (an id, no foreign key).
• The baseline (baselineKWh) and the progress come later, **asynchronously**,
  from the ConsumptionCalculated events (page //async-communication//).
end note
@enduml
